<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn al-Ash'ath</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 704</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn al-Ash'ath was an Arab nobleman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a> who led a great revolt against the Umayyad governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hajjaj-ibn-yusuf">al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf</a> from 700 to 703. Sent with a large army against the Zunbils of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, he turned it against al-Hajjaj and marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, winning wide support. He was defeated at Dayr al-Jamajim and died in 704 after taking refuge with the Zunbil.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-al-ashath.jpg" alt="Ibn al-Ash'ath" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unkown, 8th-century mint-master; photo by CNG · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirham_of_Sistan,_AH_82.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
